{"authored" [{"question" "q-127755" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Which of the matrices below does **not** have an inverse?\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0\\end{aligned}],\\,B=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 0\\end{aligned}],\\,C=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 2\\end{aligned}].\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13975082/state.json" "file_sha256" "6eec2d798dc7f5a72f06bc5a6741714b2bc2facc2c86f711dc7387c957724ae9" "basis" 766 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13975082/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-127755" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "- The matrix $A$ is a $1\\times 2$ matrix. So, it is not invertible.\n\n- For the matrix $B$, we have\n\n$$\ndet(B)=0\\cdot 0-(-1)\\cdot 1=1.\n$$\n\nBecause $det(B)\\ne 0,$ we conclude that $B$ is invertible.\n\n- For the matrix $C$, we have\n\n$$\ndet(C)=1\\cdot 2-2\\cdot 1=0.\n$$\n\nBecause $det(C)=0,$ we conclude that $C$ is not invertible.\n\nTherefore, only $A$ and $C$ do not have an inverse." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13975082/state.json" "file_sha256" "6eec2d798dc7f5a72f06bc5a6741714b2bc2facc2c86f711dc7387c957724ae9" "basis" 766 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13975082/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-127755" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13975082/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "813d2525e7300acba1c5741f8f251e0c556c58d8bdbd4e492941c9e96ab90782" "basis" 766 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13975082/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-127755" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13975082/state.json" "file_sha256" "6eec2d798dc7f5a72f06bc5a6741714b2bc2facc2c86f711dc7387c957724ae9" "basis" 766 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13975082/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-127755" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/text "$A$ and $B$ only"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13975082/state.json" "file_sha256" "6eec2d798dc7f5a72f06bc5a6741714b2bc2facc2c86f711dc7387c957724ae9" "basis" 766 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13975082/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-127755" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/text "$A$ and $C$ only"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13975082/state.json" "file_sha256" "6eec2d798dc7f5a72f06bc5a6741714b2bc2facc2c86f711dc7387c957724ae9" "basis" 766 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13975082/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-127755" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/text "$A$ only"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13975082/state.json" "file_sha256" "6eec2d798dc7f5a72f06bc5a6741714b2bc2facc2c86f711dc7387c957724ae9" "basis" 766 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13975082/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-127755" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/text "$B$ only"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13975082/state.json" "file_sha256" "6eec2d798dc7f5a72f06bc5a6741714b2bc2facc2c86f711dc7387c957724ae9" "basis" 766 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13975082/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-127755" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/text "$C$ only"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13975082/state.json" "file_sha256" "6eec2d798dc7f5a72f06bc5a6741714b2bc2facc2c86f711dc7387c957724ae9" "basis" 766 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13975082/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-71969" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "If $M=[\\begin{aligned}t & 4 \\\\ t & 10\\end{aligned}]$ is a singular matrix, calculate the value of $t.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13975082/state.json" "file_sha256" "6eec2d798dc7f5a72f06bc5a6741714b2bc2facc2c86f711dc7387c957724ae9" "basis" 766 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13975082/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-71969" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The matrix $M$ is singular if and only if $det(M)=0.$ Calculating the determinant, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(M) & =t\\cdot 10-t\\cdot 4 \\\\  & =10t-4t \\\\  & =6t\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we set the determinant equal to $0$ and solve for $t:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}6t & =0 \\\\ t & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the value of $t$ is $t=0.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13975082/state.json" "file_sha256" "6eec2d798dc7f5a72f06bc5a6741714b2bc2facc2c86f711dc7387c957724ae9" "basis" 766 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13975082/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-71969" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13975082/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "813d2525e7300acba1c5741f8f251e0c556c58d8bdbd4e492941c9e96ab90782" "basis" 766 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13975082/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-71969" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13975082/state.json" "file_sha256" "6eec2d798dc7f5a72f06bc5a6741714b2bc2facc2c86f711dc7387c957724ae9" "basis" 766 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13975082/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-71969" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "t=-5"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13975082/state.json" "file_sha256" "6eec2d798dc7f5a72f06bc5a6741714b2bc2facc2c86f711dc7387c957724ae9" "basis" 766 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13975082/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-71969" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "t=-\\frac{3}{4}"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13975082/state.json" "file_sha256" "6eec2d798dc7f5a72f06bc5a6741714b2bc2facc2c86f711dc7387c957724ae9" "basis" 766 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13975082/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-71969" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "t=0"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13975082/state.json" "file_sha256" "6eec2d798dc7f5a72f06bc5a6741714b2bc2facc2c86f711dc7387c957724ae9" "basis" 766 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13975082/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-71969" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "t=5"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13975082/state.json" "file_sha256" "6eec2d798dc7f5a72f06bc5a6741714b2bc2facc2c86f711dc7387c957724ae9" "basis" 766 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13975082/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-71969" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "t=\\frac{3}{4}"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13975082/state.json" "file_sha256" "6eec2d798dc7f5a72f06bc5a6741714b2bc2facc2c86f711dc7387c957724ae9" "basis" 766 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13975082/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-71934" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Which of the matrices below does **not** have an inverse?\n\n$$\nR=[\\begin{aligned}5 & 2 \\\\ 10 & 4\\end{aligned}],\\,S=[\\begin{aligned}15 & 0 \\\\ 1 & -1 \\\\ 10 & 0\\end{aligned}],\\,T=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 2 \\\\ -2 & 2\\end{aligned}].\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13979417/state.json" "file_sha256" "5c883a2e5de1eeebb6a3e52c4ea740ce8fa1bb3890e192b9895aff80945bcf13" "basis" 851 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13979417/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-71934" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "- For the matrix $R$, we have\n\n$$\ndet(R)=5\\cdot 4-10\\cdot 2=0.\n$$\n\nBecause $det(R)=0,$ we conclude that $R$ is not invertible.\n\n- The matrix $S$ is a $3\\times 2$ matrix. So, it is not invertible.\n\n- For the matrix $T$, we have\n\n$$\ndet(T)=2\\cdot 2-(-2)\\cdot 2=8.\n$$\n\nBecause $det(T)\\ne 0,$ we conclude that $T$ is invertible.\n\nTherefore, only $R$ and $S$ do not have an inverse." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13979417/state.json" "file_sha256" "5c883a2e5de1eeebb6a3e52c4ea740ce8fa1bb3890e192b9895aff80945bcf13" "basis" 851 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13979417/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-71934" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13979417/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "5e145fb97abb632207d6c68caf0fb1c3e75e785931de38c4da626620ab90b1a2" "basis" 851 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13979417/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-71934" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13979417/state.json" "file_sha256" "5c883a2e5de1eeebb6a3e52c4ea740ce8fa1bb3890e192b9895aff80945bcf13" "basis" 851 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13979417/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-71934" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/text "$R$ and $S$ only"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13979417/state.json" "file_sha256" "5c883a2e5de1eeebb