singular.\n\n- The matrix $B$ is a $1\\times 2$ matrix. So, it is not invertible. Since the matrix is not square, we can't say that it's singular.\n\n- For the matrix $C$, we have\n\n$$\ndet(C)=1\\cdot 5-7\\cdot 0=5.\n$$\n\nBecause $det(C)\\ne 0,$ we conclude that $C$ is invertible.\n\nTherefore, only $A$ is singular." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13991694/state.json" "file_sha256" "58ff567c65138cf3abcd2c1b02bc455e98c0d2c0285f34e374c23da418e6f72e" "basis" 1033 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13991694/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-127821" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13991694/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "b8a338119d773f18183b964e1d0ec6c948d1b5ea5ebaaac0f518e848bed090ec" "basis" 1033 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13991694/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-127821" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13991694/state.json" "file_sha256" "58ff567c65138cf3abcd2c1b02bc455e98c0d2c0285f34e374c23da418e6f72e" "basis" 1033 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13991694/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-127821" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/text "$A$  and $C$ only"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13991694/state.json" "file_sha256" "58ff567c65138cf3abcd2c1b02bc455e98c0d2c0285f34e374c23da418e6f72e" "basis" 1033 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13991694/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-127821" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/text "$A$ only"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13991694/state.json" "file_sha256" "58ff567c65138cf3abcd2c1b02bc455e98c0d2c0285f34e374c23da418e6f72e" "basis" 1033 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13991694/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-127821" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/text "$B$  and $C$ only"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13991694/state.json" "file_sha256" "58ff567c65138cf3abcd2c1b02bc455e98c0d2c0285f34e374c23da418e6f72e" "basis" 1033 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13991694/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-127821" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/text "$B$ only"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13991694/state.json" "file_sha256" "58ff567c65138cf3abcd2c1b02bc455e98c0d2c0285f34e374c23da418e6f72e" "basis" 1033 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13991694/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-127821" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/text "$C$ only"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13991694/state.json" "file_sha256" "58ff567c65138cf3abcd2c1b02bc455e98c0d2c0285f34e374c23da418e6f72e" "basis" 1033 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13991694/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-127821" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/text "$A$ only"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13991694/state.json" "file_sha256" "58ff567c65138cf3abcd2c1b02bc455e98c0d2c0285f34e374c23da418e6f72e" "basis" 1033 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13991694/edb-import/verification.json"}] "sources" [{"question" "q-71934" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Which of the matrices below does **not** have an inverse?\n\n$$\nR=[\\begin{aligned}5 & 2 \\\\ 10 & 4\\end{aligned}],\\,S=[\\begin{aligned}15 & 0 \\\\ 1 & -1 \\\\ 10 & 0\\end{aligned}],\\,T=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 2 \\\\ -2 & 2\\end{aligned}].\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14042464/state.json" "file_sha256" "f6f8504cc0ffb646474e66a00b6bb202b1de01e812ecf2bfcfd4195de85ebf18"} {"question" "q-71934" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "- For the matrix $R$, we have\n\n$$\ndet(R)=5\\cdot 4-10\\cdot 2=0.\n$$\n\nBecause $det(R)=0,$ we conclude that $R$ is not invertible.\n\n- The matrix $S$ is a $3\\times 2$ matrix. So, it is not invertible.\n\n- For the matrix $T$, we have\n\n$$\ndet(T)=2\\cdot 2-(-2)\\cdot 2=8.\n$$\n\nBecause $det(T)\\ne 0,$ we conclude that $T$ is invertible.\n\nTherefore, only $R$ and $S$ do not have an inverse." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14042464/state.json" "file_sha256" "f6f8504cc0ffb646474e66a00b6bb202b1de01e812ecf2bfcfd4195de85ebf18"} {"question" "q-71934" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14042464/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "74e258f47cef38d5231d860b9951c8d2a779b55734d2e674f79b3ee0f3650ae5"} {"question" "q-71934" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14042464/state.json" "file_sha256" "f6f8504cc0ffb646474e66a00b6bb202b1de01e812ecf2bfcfd4195de85ebf18"} {"question" "q-71934" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["text" "$R$ and $S$ only"] ["text" "$R$ and $T$ only"] ["text" "$R$ only"] ["text" "$S$ only"] ["text" "$T$ only"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14042464/state.json" "file_sha256" "f6f8504cc0ffb646474e66a00b6bb202b1de01e812ecf2bfcfd4195de85ebf18"} {"question" "q-71934" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/text "$R$ and $S$ only"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14042464/state.json" "file_sha256" "f6f8504cc0ffb646474e66a00b6bb202b1de01e812ecf2bfcfd4195de85ebf18"} {"question" "q-71969" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "If $M=[\\begin{aligned}t & 4 \\\\ t & 10\\end{aligned}]$ is a singular matrix, calculate the value of $t.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14042464/state.json" "file_sha256" "f6f8504cc0ffb646474e66a00b6bb202b1de01e812ecf2bfcfd4195de85ebf18"} {"question" "q-71969" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The matrix $M$ is singular if and only if $det(M)=0.$ Calculating the determinant, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(M) & =t\\cdot 10-t\\cdot 4 \\\\  & =10t-4t \\\\  & =6t\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we set the determinant equal to $0$ and solve for $t:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}6t & =0 \\\\ t & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the value of $t$ is $t=0.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14042464/state.json" "file_sha256" "f6f8504cc0ffb646474e66a00b6bb202b1de01e812ecf2bfcfd4195de85ebf18"} {"question" "q-71969" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14042464/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "74e258f47cef38d5231d860b9951c8d2a779b55734d2e674f79b3ee0f3650ae5"} {"question" "q-71969" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14042464/state.json" "file_sha256" "f6f8504cc0ffb646474e66a00b6bb202b1de01e812ecf2bfcfd4195de85ebf18"} {"question" "q-71969" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "t=-5"] ["math" "t=-\\frac{3}{4}"] ["math" "t=0"] ["math" "t=5"] ["math" "t=\\frac{3}{4}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14042464/state.json" "file_sha256" "f6f8504cc0ffb646474e66a00b6bb202b1de01e812ecf2bfcfd4195de85ebf18"} {"question" "q-71969" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "t=0"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14042464/state.json" "file_sha256" "f6f8504cc0ffb646474e66a00b6bb202b1de01e812ecf2bfcfd4195de85ebf18"} {"question" "q-127755" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Which of the matrices below does **not** have an inverse?\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0\\end{aligned}],\\,B=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 0\\end{aligned}],\\,C=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 2\\end{aligned}].\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14042464/state.json" "file_sha256" "f6f8504cc0ffb646474e66a00b6bb202b1de01e812ecf2bfcfd4195de85ebf18"} {"question" "q-127755" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "- The matrix $A$ is a $1\\times 2$ matrix. So, it is not invertible.\n\n- For the matrix $B$, we have\n\n$$\ndet(B)=0\\cdot 0-(-1)\\cdot 1=1.\n$$\n\nBecause $det(B)\\ne 0,$ we conclude that $B$ is invertible.\n\n- For the matrix $C$, we have\n\n$$\ndet(C)=1\\cdot 2-2\\cdot 1=0.\n$$\n\nBecause $det(C)=0,$ we conclude that $C$ is not invertible.\n\nTherefore, only $A$ and $C$ do not have an inverse." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14042464/state.json" "file_sha256" "f6f8504cc0ffb646474e66a00b6bb202b1de01e812ecf2bfcfd4195de85ebf18"} {"question" "q-127755" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14042464/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "74e258f47cef38d5231d860b9951c8d2a779b55734d2e674f79b3ee0f3650ae5"} {"question" "q-127755" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14042464/state.json" "file_sha256" "f6f8504cc0ffb646474e66a00b6bb202b1de01e812ecf2bfcfd4195de85ebf18"} {"question" "q-127755" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["text" "$A$ and $B$ only"] ["text" "$A$ and $C$ only"] ["text" "$A$ only"] ["text" "$B$ only"] ["text" "$C$ only"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14042464/state.json" "file_sha256" "f6f8504cc0ffb646474e66a00b6bb202b1de01e812ecf2bfcfd4195de85ebf18"} {"question" "q-127755" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/text "$A$ and $C$ only"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14042464/state.json" "file_sha256" "f6f8504cc0ffb646474e66a00b6bb202b1de01e812ecf2bfcfd4195de85ebf18"} {"question" "q-127821" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Which of the matrices below are singular?\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 6 \\\\ 1 & -3\\end{aligned}],\\,B=[\\begin{aligned}-3 & 1\\end{aligned}],\\,C=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 7 & 5\\end{aligned}].\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14042464/state.json" "file_sha256" "f6f8504cc0ffb646474e66a00b6bb202b1de01e812ecf2bfcfd4195de85ebf18"} {"question" "q-127821" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "- For the matrix $A$, we have\n\n$$\ndet(A)=-2\\cdot (-3)-1\\cdot 6=0.\n$$\n\nBecause $det(A)=0,$ we conclude that $A$ is not invertible. Since $A$ is a square matrix that is not invertible, we also say that $A$ is singular.\n\n- The matrix $B$ is a $1\\times 2$ matrix. So, it is not invertible. Since the matrix is not square, we can't say that it's singular.\n\n- For the matrix $C$, we have\n\n$$\ndet(C)=1\\cdot 5-7\\cdot 0=5.\n$$\n\nBecause $det(C)\\ne 0,$ we conclude that $C$ is invertible.\n\nTherefore, only $A$ is singular." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14042464/state.json" "file_sha256" "f6f8504cc0ffb646474e66a00b6bb202b1de01e812ecf2bfcfd4195de85ebf18"} {"question" "q-127821" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14042464/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "74e258f47cef38d5231d860b9951c8d2a779b55734d2e674f79b3ee0f3650ae5"} {"question" "q-127821" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14042464/state.json" "file_sha256" "f6f8504cc0ffb646474e66a00b6bb202b1de01e812ecf2bfcfd4195de85ebf18"} {"question" "q-127821" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["text" "$A$  and $C$ only"] ["text" "$A$ only"] ["text" "$B$  and $C$ only"] ["text" "$B$ only"] ["text" "$C$ only"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14042464/state.json" "file_sha256" "f6f8504cc0ffb646474e66a00b6bb202b1de01e812ecf2bfcfd4195de85ebf18"} {"question" "q-127821" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/text "$A$ only"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14042464/state.json" "file_sha256" "f6f8504cc0ffb646474e66a00b6bb202b1de01e812ecf2bfcfd4195de85ebf18"} {"question" "q-127903" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "If $M=[\\begin{aligned}t & 5 \\\\ t & 9\\end{aligned}]$ is a singular matrix, calculate the value(s) of $t.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14042464/state.json" "file_sha256" "f6f8504cc0ffb646474e66a00b6bb202b1de01e812ecf2bfcfd4195de85ebf18"} {"question" "q-127903" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The matrix $M$ is singular if and only if $det(M)=0.$ Calculating the determinant, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(M) & =t\\cdot 9-t\\cdot 5 \\\\  & =9t-5t \\\\  & =4t\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we set the determinant equal to $0$ and solve for $t:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4t & =0 \\\\ t & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the value of $t$ is $t=0.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14042464/state.json" "file_sha256" "f6f8504cc0ffb646474e66a00b6bb202b1de01e812ecf2bfcfd4195de85ebf18"} {"question" "q-127903" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14042464/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "74e258f47cef38d5231d860b9951c8d2a779b55734d2e674f79b3ee0f3650ae5"} {"question" "q-127903" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14042464/state.json" "file_sha256" "f6f8504cc0ffb646474e66a00b6bb202b1de01e812ecf2bfcfd4195de85ebf18"} {"question" "q-127903" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "k=\\pm 10"] ["math" "k=\\pm 7"] ["math" "t=0"] ["math" "t=4"] ["math" "t=9"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14042464/state.json" "file_sha256" "f6f8504cc0ffb646474e66a00b6bb202b1de01e812ecf2bfcfd4195de85ebf18"} {"question" "q-127903" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "t=0"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14042464/state.json" "file_sha256" "f6f8504cc0ffb646474e66a00b6bb202b1de01e812ecf2bfcfd4195de85ebf18"}] "usage" {"q-127821" [] "q-127903" [] "q-71969" [] "q-127755" [] "q-71934" []} "basis" 1566 "retractions" [] "immutable_answers" [17592186277084 17592186277085 17592186277086 17592186277087 17592186277088 17592186277129 17592186277130 17592186277131 17592186277132 17592186277133 17592186279753 17592186279754 17592186279755 17592186279756 17